Job Title:
Accountant
Posting Start Date:
9/3/26
Job Description:
It’s never been a more exciting time to join Vistra.
At Vistra our purpose is progress. We believe that our clients have the power to change the world and to do great things for global progress, and we exist to remove the friction that comes from the complexity of global business – to help our clients achieve progress without friction.
But progress only happens when people come together and take action. And we’re absolutely committed to building a culture where our people can do just that.
We have an exciting opportunity for you to join our team as an Accountant . This full-time and permanent position is based in Bulgaria (Sofia) .
Responsibilities:
Entering information in electronic form or from paper carrier in the accounting software;
Processing the entered information and allocating it in respective files and folders in electronic form or on paper carrier;
Extracting information from the databases;
Registering the accounting operations in chronological order;
Preparing primary and secondary accounting documents;
Preparing monthly VAT reporting and returns;
Preparing monthly, quarterly and annual management reports in accordance with international standards and internal requirements;
Assisting with financial and tax audit of clients;
Maintaining correspondence and communication with clients;
Participating in stock-taking and checks of accountable persons;
Communicating with NRA, NSSI and other institutions;
Assisting the other departments for the purpose of providing better services for clients;
Filling-in timesheets for the worked-off time;
Independently or in a team, performs other tasks assigned by the line manager.
Requirements:
University degree in Accounting, Finance or any other relevant discipline;
At least 2+ years accounting experience;
Excellent command of Bulgarian language and good command of English language;
Very good knowledge of the Bulgarian accounting and tax legislation;
Good computer literacy - MS Word, Excel, Outlook;
Experience with working on different ERP Systems;
Excellent organizational and interpersonal skills;
Fast learning person, with a good eye for details;
High motivation to achieve results and seek solutions.
We are offering:
Opportunity to gain an experience in an international company well-established on the market;
Positive team of professionals;
Attractive start remuneration;
Yearly performance evaluation plan;
Additional Health Insurance;
Multisport Cards;
Food vouchers;
Additional retirement plan;
Hybrid working model;
Challenges and career prospects.
In addition to the professional education and qualifications, we seek a proactive, honest and affable person to support our corporate culture.
If you are interested in joining Vistra please send your CV in English.
